---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
const pageSlug = 'encrypt-files-on-android';
const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Encrypting files on Android',
  description: 'How file encryption works on Android phones and how Vireault applies AES-256-GCM locally.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vireault' },
  datePublished: '2026-11-05',
  dateModified: '2026-11-05',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://vireault.app/guides/encrypt-files-on-android',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Encrypting files on Android"
  description="A plain-language guide to encrypting files on Android, covering AES-256-GCM, key derivation, backups and common mistakes."
  path="/guides/encrypt-files-on-android"
  pageSlug={pageSlug}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={articleLd}
  article={{ published: '2026-11-05', modified: '2026-11-05' }}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/guides', label: 'Guides' }, { label: 'Encrypt files' }]} />
    <article class="section prose">
      <h1>Encrypting files on Android</h1>
      <p>Full-disk encryption protects a powered-off phone, but it does not stop someone who unlocks your device from opening the gallery. App-level file encryption adds a second gate around specific private documents and media.</p>
      <h2>The pieces that matter</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Key derivation</strong> — turns a PIN, pattern or passphrase into cryptographic material (Vireault: Argon2id)</li>
        <li><strong>Master key</strong> — a random key that actually encrypts file bytes</li>
        <li><strong>Authenticated encryption</strong> — AES-256-GCM protects confidentiality and detects tampering</li>
        <li><strong>Encrypted index</strong> — keeps names from leaking beside the ciphertext</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Assuming “hidden” equals “encrypted”</li>
        <li>Leaving gallery originals after import</li>
        <li>Storing recovery material inside the same unlocked photo roll</li>
        <li>Skipping backups because the vault “feels permanent”</li>
      </ul>
      <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} heading="Encrypt files without creating an account" body="Vireault keeps ciphertext local and lets you export an encrypted backup file when you need a spare copy." />
      <h2>Backup without undoing encryption</h2>
      <p>Copying raw vault directories around is risky if you do not understand the format. Prefer the app’s <a href="/features/backup-restore">encrypted backup and restore</a> flow, then store that file deliberately.</p>
      <h2>How this ties to Vireault features</h2>
      <p>Read the <a href="/features/encryption">encryption page</a>, the <a href="/features/offline">offline design</a>, and the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> for product specifics. For category shopping, use the <a href="/guides/safest-private-gallery-android">private gallery checklist</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
